{"lines": [["title", "We are team Minus Zero: Ahmad Farruk Towsif and MD Toslim Uddin Rahat. Our project is Mission Architect, built for the Space Mission Design Game challenge."], ["problem", "Real space missions take years and huge teams to design, so students never get to feel how mission design actually works \u2014 how one choice about fuel, power or money decides whether a mission lives or dies."], ["solution", "Mission Architect turns that into a game anyone can play in a browser."], ["build", "You pick a destination \u2014 the Moon, Mars, or asteroid Bennu \u2014 choose a real rocket and engine, and build your spacecraft part by part."], ["equation", "A real rocket equation checks your delta-v live."], ["blocked", "Too heavy, no power, not enough fuel \u2014 the game will not let you launch, and it tells you why in plain language."], ["flight", "In flight, real dangers strike: solar flares, dust storms, equipment failures. Whether you survive depends on what you built."], ["results", "Every mission ends with a grade and a debrief that explains your own decisions."], ["anywhere", "It runs in any browser, on a phone or a computer, by mouse or keyboard."], ["nasa", "Our game runs on real NASA data: the NASA Open Science Data Repository, including radiation data; NASA Planetary Fact Sheets for distance, gravity and delta-v; the NASA JPL Small-Body Database for asteroid Bennu; and NASA DONKI space-weather data behind our solar flare events."], ["close", "Mission Architect \u2014 design it, build it, fly it. Play it live \u2014 the link is on our project page."]], "words": [["we", 1.18, 1.42], ["are", 1.42, 1.5], ["team", 1.5, 1.81], ["minus", 1.81, 2.25], ["zero(2)", 2.25, 2.59], ["ahmad", 3.44, 3.77], ["farruk", 3.77, 4.12], ["towsif", 4.12, 4.72], ["and", 5.08, 5.33], ["md", 5.47, 5.82], ["toslim", 5.82, 6.41], ["uddin", 6.41, 6.64], ["rahat", 6.64, 6.91], ["our(3)", 8.1, 8.29], ["project(2)", 8.29, 8.74], ["is", 8.74, 9.05], ["mission", 9.23, 9.67], ["architec